# MANDATORY: TRANSOVO IA & Navigation Standards (Guide #3)

**Source of truth:** `docs/TRANSOVO-IA-NAVIGATION-STANDARDS.md`

## Hard requirement

Any nav, routing, labeling, or feature placement change **MUST** comply with this guide. Read the full document first.

## Non-negotiables

- **One canonical home** per feature — no duplicate permanent nav entries.
- Use **canonical terminology** — same object, same name everywhere.
- Top-level IA follows approved structure (Home, Appointments, Booking, Contacts, Messages, Automations, Meetings, Payments, Analytics, Integrations, Settings).
- **Local navigation** belongs inside the feature — not new top-level items for convenience.
- Breadcrumbs and back links preserve **context**, not duplicate IA.
- Nav changes go through `src/lib/products/` patterns — no scattered hardcoded conditionals.
- Mobile nav must expose the same authoritative destinations — not a divergent product.

## On conflict

Governance and product scope beat local convenience.
